<section>
    <h2 class="mobile-centred-heading">Usage</h2>

    <p>
        Below, for the container I just used the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Section.Base</span> with a border and left the default padding on.
        I then just included the default <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">GridRow.Base</span> to get a grid that by default unless changed has a small gap assigned.
        The grid system like many others, has colums placed inside it that add up a predifined total such as 12. If the number of columns is exceeded new row is
        created in the grid for the column.
    </p>
    <p>
        Also like many grid systems, when the column is below its breakpoint size it will automatically take up the entire row. The example could have been made
        via the C# helpter classes, I added the style attributed to focus more on the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">GridRow.ColSpan</span>
    </p>
    <div class="@Section.Base @Section.Bordered @GridRow.Base">
        <div class="@GridRow.ColSpan(UnitBreakpoint.Md, UnitColSpan.Five)" style="padding: var(--br-unit-space-1); border:1px solid var(--br-comp-all-divider-colour);">
            colspan md 5
        </div>
        <div class="@GridRow.ColSpan(UnitBreakpoint.Md, UnitColSpan.Seven)" style="padding: var(--br-unit-space-1); border:1px solid var(--br-comp-all-divider-colour);">
            colspan md 7
        </div>
        <div class="@GridRow.ColSpan(UnitBreakpoint.Lg, UnitColSpan.Four)" style="padding: var(--br-unit-space-1); border:1px solid var(--br-comp-all-divider-colour);">
            colspan lg 4
        </div>
    </div>
    <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CssClassesSnippets.GidRow_Code_Example" AriaLabel="Grid row code example" />
</section>

